                Data sheet (Hi3520D/Hi3515A/Hi3515C data sheet issue 07 (2015-02-09)): section 5.1.6.3, Table 5-7, page 5-55, register description at text dump line 27305 (build/sdk-survey/datasheet.txt).
            ";

            enum cpuaddr_in_rdy_enum {
                CPU_CANNOT_CONFIGURE = 0x0 { desc = "The CPU cannot configure the frame header address of the RX queue."; };
                CPU_CAN_CONFIGURE = 0x1 { desc = "The CPU can configure the frame header address of the RX queue."; };
            };

            field {
                name = "cpuaddr_in_rdy";
                desc = "Indicates whether the CPU can configure the frame header address of the RX queue. Note: The values of cpuaddr_in_rdy and eq_in_rdy are set to 0 during reset. The values, however, are set to 1 by the circuit immediately after reset. In other words, after reset, the iq address queue and eq descriptor queue are configurable. Hardware-verified: reset value reads 0x03000000 (both ready bits set) and the U-Boot driver polls these bits as RECVQ_RDY/XMITQ_RDY.";
