regfile eHISI_HIETH_SF {
    name = "ETH Registers";
    desc = "
    The Ethernet (ETH) module of the Hi3520D/Hi3515A/Hi3515C (vendor name HISFV300, Linux/U-Boot driver `hieth`, a switch-fabric style Fast Ethernet MAC) receives and transmits frames at 10 or 100 Mbit/s, half or full duplex, over an MII interface to the embedded FE PHY or an external RMII PHY. It has an MDIO master with a configurable frequency, 64 frame management queues for RX and TX each, eight configurable destination MAC filter table entries, traffic limit/flow control, statistics counters and 802.3az EEE support for the embedded PHY. Frames are exchanged with memory through frame descriptors (header address and length) queued in the RX/TX queues; there is no DMA descriptor ring in memory.

    The Hi3515 (ETH at 0x10090000, VIC interrupt 14; English data sheet issue 02 (2010-04-20), register summary at `Hi3515-Datasheet.txt` line 22220; audit 2026-11-09) has the same two-port switch fabric (its summary table lists every port register at 0x0200 and 0x2200): the register set and bit layouts match this file, except that its data sheet has no EEE registers (`define HISI_HIETH_SF_NO_EEE removes MAC_EEE_INT..MAC_EEE_CLK_CNT) and adds the VLAN/MAC-limit counters VN2OTH_PKTS, VN2CPU_PKTS and MN2OTH_PKTS at 0x640-0x648 (`define HISI_HIETH_SF_VLAN_CNT adds them). Not modelled from that data sheet: MAC_SET bits 31:30 printed as a read-only field named reversed (reserved), GLB_IRQN_SET.int_frm_cnt reset printed as 0 in the bit row while its Total Reset Value header says 0x0800_003A, i.e. 8 (this file: 8, the header and the Hi3520D value), the write-1-to-clear bits marked WC (same behaviour), and the vendor-only MAC_RX_IPGCTRL/MAC_TX_IPGCTRL which it does not document.

    Second data-sheet pass 2026-11-10 (scripted field-by-field compare of every register, field, bit range, access, reset and total reset of the Hi3520D data sheet issue 02 (2013-06-21) and the Hi3515 data sheet issue 02 against this file: no register, field, access or reset mismatch). Differences that are deliberate: the down port (0x2000..0x2FFF) and every `_down` field of the GLB registers are not in either data sheet (the Hi3515 summary table only says 0x0200, 0x2200; the Hi3520D data sheet documents the up port only); they come from the vendor driver. The vendor header glb.h also defines bits that neither data sheet lists and no vendor code uses, they are not modelled: GLB_FWCTRL FW2OTHPORT_ENA/FORCE (bits 4, 6, 8, 10), GLB_MACTCTRL UNI/MULTI/BROAD2OTHPORT (bits 0, 2, 4 up; 8-12 down), GLB_MACn_H16 FW2PORT (bit 20 up, 18 down) and ENA_D (bit 16), and BITS_VLAN_IRQS (GLB_IRQ bit 11). The Hi3520D data sheet total reset of GLB_FC_LEVEL (0x3018_0508) sets bits that its field table calls reserved (modelled as reserved_nz). Both data sheets print the PHY clock/reset glue in PERI_CRG51 (Hi3520D: eth_rmiick_sel[4], mii_rmii_mode[3], fephy_srst_req[2], eth_cken[1], hrst_eth_s[0], reset 0x2; RDL matches) and, on the Hi3515, SC_PERCTRL8[18] eth_srst plus the ethclken/ethclkdis/ethclkstat bits [21] of SC_PERCLKEN/DIS/STAT. Hi3520D interrupts: ETH = GIC SPI 24 (interrupt bit 56), FE PHY = SPI 25 (bit 57).

    ## Layout

    | Offset | Block |
    |--------|-------|
    | 0x0000 | up port registers (`UP`: MDIO status/mask, MAC, queue, EEE, counters) |
    | 0x1100 | MDIO command and read-data registers (`MDIO`) |
    | 0x1300 | global registers and MAC filter table (`GLB`) |
    | 0x2000 | down port registers (`DOWN`, same layout as `UP`) |

    The internal fast Ethernet PHY registers (BMCR, BMSR, ..., 0x00-0x1F, described in the data sheet at lines 28711-29600) are not part of this register space: they are reached through the MDIO master, so they are not described here.

    !!! NOTE
        Hardware-verified with the U-Boot `hieth_sf` driver on a Hi3520D: MDIO_RWCTRL bit 15 is the command-finished flag, read data is at +0x1104, the global block is at +0x1300 and the queue registers U_GLB_QLEN_SET/IQFRM_DES/IQ_ADDR/EQ_ADDR/EQFRM_LEN/ADDRQ_STAT are at 0x344/0x354/0x358/0x360/0x364/0x36C of the up port.
    ";

    eHISI_HIETH_SF_PORT UP   @ 0x0000;
    eHISI_HIETH_SF_MDIO MDIO @ 0x1100;
    eHISI_HIETH_SF_GLB  GLB  @ 0x1300;
    eHISI_HIETH_SF_PORT DOWN @ 0x2000;
};

`endif
